{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"APPLY AUTHORIZATION + PROVENANCE (recorded so the chain is tracker-visible rather than living only in agent context).\n\nThe terraform apply for this ticket is pre-authorized. The authorization did NOT originate in the store: the operator approved it in response to the apply-pending framing, and it reached me via a coordinator relay of that approval. This comment's own timestamp is the authoritative date of the relay; the underlying alarm sweep it came from is the 2026-08-12 AWS investigation recorded on childsafe-bizarre-lorikeet (b902-18af-14ed-4da1) comment 12.\n\nRecording this because the earlier lorikeet record lists both follow-ups as 'surfaced for operator decision' with no written approval in the store -- so without this note the apply would look self-authorized on a later read.\n\nDIVISION OF LABOUR, as relayed: the COORDINATOR runs the apply after change 1688 merges, inspecting the plan first. I do not touch AWS. When the coordinator confirms the apply, I tick AC5 and close this ticket fully; until that confirmation arrives the ticket stays in_progress.\n\nEXPECTED PLAN for the coordinator to verify against -- 3 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy:\n  + aws_iam_role.gha_bridge_metrics              (rebar-bridge-metrics)\n  + aws_iam_role_policy.gha_bridge_metrics_put   (rebar-bridge-metrics-put; cloudwatch:PutMetricData conditioned on cloudwatch:namespace = rebar/host)\n  + aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.bridge_run_failures  (rebar-bridge-run-failures)\n  plus a new output, bridge_metrics_role_arn.\n\nAnything beyond those three adds -- in particular ANY diff against aws_iam_role.gha_terraform_plan, its attached policies, or the Bedrock role -- means this change widened an existing role and the plan should be rejected rather than applied.\n\nPOST-APPLY, before AC5 can be ticked: set repo Variables AWS_BRIDGE_METRICS_ROLE_ARN (= terraform output bridge_metrics_role_arn) and AWS_BRIDGE_METRICS_REGION. The workflow skips its metric steps while either is unset, so the metric only begins flowing once both exist. Proof for AC5: aws cloudwatch describe-alarms --alarm-names rebar-bridge-run-failures returns the alarm."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786576501854618001,"uuid":"5a2f0fe5-fa40-41fb-b46d-cd986086325c"}